{
  "title": "Shift aesthetic from generic dark dashboard to warm editorial cookbook",
  "description": "Right now the app reads as \"Vite starter dark theme\" — \
cool #1a1a1a surfaces, #646cff indigo accent, single geometric sans \
everywhere. Nothing signals \"cookbook\" or \"food.\"\n\
\n\
Goals:\n\
- **Typography pairing**: pick a distinctive display serif (Fraunces, GT \
  Sectra, DM Serif Display, Redaction, Domaine) for titles/headings, and \
  a characterful sans for body (not Inter/Roboto). Italic variants for the \
  recipe title area.\n\
- **Color system**: warm the near-blacks (e.g. app `#120f0d`, card \
  `#1a1614`, elevated `#221d1a`). Replace indigo as the primary accent with a \
  warmer hue (saffron/turmeric around #e8a33d works well); reserve a deep \
  cherry for destructive actions. Apply the warm accent sparingly — primary \
  CTA + selection state only — not to every border.\n\
- **Photo treatment**: drop (or hairline) the card border, let photos bleed \
  to the card edge, rounded corners on the card rather than the inner \
  thumbnail.\n\
- **Hover/interaction**: replace the generic 4px lift with something quieter \
  (slow inset scale of the photo, or a revealed serif-italic \"View →\" tag). \
  Keep a clear focus ring for keyboard users.\n\
- **Texture**: optional subtle paper-grain noise on the body background \
  (<3% opacity). Gate on `prefers-reduced-motion` / OLED concerns with a \
  toggle if needed.\n\
\n\
Ship this as one PR so it reads as an intentional redesign, not a drift.\n\
\n\
CSS quality: this is the right moment to introduce real design tokens as \
CSS custom properties (`--surface-0`, `--surface-1`, `--accent`, \
`--accent-destructive`, `--text-primary`, `--text-muted`, `--font-display`, \
`--font-body`, etc.). There are ~200 hardcoded color literals in App.css \
today — a lot of this change is deleting those in favor of the new tokens. \
Don't leave both systems coexisting. See `p3-css-cleanup.json5`.",
